        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "15be60d2-ddae-59c2-b829-e0eee3b718bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leon Uris\n- Products: Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, Exodus, Trinity, The Haj\n- Places: Berlin, Germany, East Berlin, East Germany\n- Events: World War II, Berlin Airlift\n- Concepts: historical fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Uris was born on August 3, 1924, and he became an American author known for historical fiction.\n- Armageddon, also titled Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, is a novel by Leon Uris about post-World War II Berlin and Germany.\n- Armageddon includes a vivid description of the Berlin Airlift and portrays interactions among people from five nations, including the three major Western Allies and the Soviet occupiers of East Berlin and East Germany.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Exodus in 1958.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Trinity in 1976.\n- Leon Uris published The Haj in 1984, a novel about a Palestinian Arab family living through historic events in the 1920s to 1950s as witnessed by Ishmael, the youngest son.\n- Leon Uris died on June 21, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "71a1a916-0af6-5cdf-afc8-7f26f9932371",
        "text": "Page: Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin. Sentence: Armageddon, or Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, is a novel by Leon Uris about post-World War II Berlin and Germany.\nPage: Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin. Sentence: The description of the Berlin Airlift is quite vivid as is the inter-action between people of the five nations involved as the three major Western Allies rub along with the Soviet occupiers of East Berlin and East Germany.\nPage: Leon Uris. Sentence: Leon Marcus Uris (August 3, 1924 – June 21, 2003) was an American author, known for his historical fiction.\nPage: Leon Uris. Sentence: His two bestselling books were \"Exodus\" (published in 1958) and \"Trinity\" (published in 1976).\nPage: The Haj. Sentence: The Haj is a novel published in 1984 by American author Leon Uris about a Palestinian Arab family caught up in the area's historic events of the 1920s–1950s as witnessed by Ishmael, the youngest son.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
